#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab
────────────────────────────────────────
S3: Object Versioning with MinIO

Scenario
  A configuration object already exists in an S3-compatible bucket, but
  bucket versioning is disabled. A new revision must be published without
  losing the previous object revision.

Goal
  1. Inspect the current bucket versioning state.
  2. Enable bucket versioning.
  3. Upload /workspace/config-v2.json to app/config.json.
  4. Prove that at least two versions exist and revision 2 is latest.

Useful commands
  aws s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket kh-lab-bucket
  aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket kh-lab-bucket --prefix app/config.json
  cat /workspace/config-v2.json

Lab commands
  help      show this assignment again
  status    show MinIO and current versioning state
  check     validate the current solution
  hint      reveal the next progressive hint
  reset     restore the original unversioned state
  labs      list all bundled labs

Note
  MinIO is S3-compatible local training infrastructure, not a real AWS account.
EOF
